      "writtenOn": "2021-03-18T01:49:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The existence of this code suggests that the set of redactions should not be a property of TransportInfo, but a property of NetworkCapabilities. Because even if the transportinfo says \"I don\u0027t need or support any redactions\", other data in NetworkCapabilities might.\n\nA great example of this is the SSID field in NetworkCapabilities. Currently this field is cleared unconditionally if the receiver does not have NETWORK_SETTINGS. In reality, it seems more correct to redact that field based on location.\n\nSo perhaps we should move these redaction constants to NetworkCapabilities? TransportInfo can still use and understand them, take them as arguments, etc. In practice, I think this is already the case in this CL, because the NetworkCapabilities copy constructor takes a bitmask of redactions.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1949,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1951,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "3ae037e96b7a251493ec07631de719ca196ae231",
